# Noty Linux — attribution notice

Noty Linux is an independent Linux desktop implementation. Its interaction
idea and early visual references were inspired by [Noty for macOS by Aymen
Hamza](https://github.com/aimen08/noty), which is MIT-licensed. KDE Plasma is
the first shipping desktop integration.

This repository does not contain the upstream Swift, SwiftUI or AppKit source,
nor does it present itself as an official release or endorsement from the
upstream author. The KDE implementation is written in Qt 6, QML and C++.

The bundled action icons are [Phosphor Icons](https://phosphoricons.com/) in
the Regular weight. Their MIT license is included in
[`licenses/PHOSPHOR-MIT.txt`](licenses/PHOSPHOR-MIT.txt).

The landing page self-hosts Noto Serif under the SIL Open Font License 1.1.
Its complete license text is included in
[`licenses/NOTO-OFL.txt`](licenses/NOTO-OFL.txt).
